  "final_message": "I will check the repository structure and implementation details.\nI will wait for the file listing to complete.\nI will wait for the search to complete.\nI will wait for the search task to complete.\nI will wait for the test suite to run.\nI will wait for the test run to finish.\nI will wait for the test run to complete.\nI will wait for the test run to finish.\nI will wait for the tests to finish.\nI will wait for the test task notification.\nI will wait for the architecture check to complete.\nI will wait for the architecture check result.\nI will wait for the typecheck command to finish.\nI will wait for the typecheck result.\nI will wait for git status to complete.\nI will wait for git status output.\nI will wait for git diff output.\nI will wait for git diff output.\nTo align `OrderPlaced` event naming with the Payments and Customer APIs while complying with architecture rule **ARCH-4** (*\"No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation\"*), the following changes were implemented:\n\n1. **Additive Rename with Deprecation in [`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L66)**:\n   - Added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L34) event interface and populated them in [`orderPlaced()`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L52-L66).\n   - Retained `totalCents` and `placedAt` marked as `@deprecated` to ensure deployed downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) continue functioning seamlessly without breaking changes.\n2. **Updated Unit & Integration Tests**:\n   - Updated event assertions in [`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/test/app.test.ts#L21-L53) and [`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/test/adapters.test.ts#L47-L52) to verify both the newly aligned fields and the deprecated compatibility fields.\n\nAll tests (`npm test`), architecture rule validations (`npm run arch`), and TypeScript type checks (`npm run typecheck`) pass successfully.\n",
